{"_v":1,"id":"the-country-girl-2008","bd":{"positive":1,"mixed":1,"negative":1},"rv":[{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2008/legit/reviews/the-country-girl-1200472139/","d":"2008-04-28","q":"The two plays are worlds apart: The politics, richly populated ensemble and pinpoint sociology of the early work gave way to a more sentimental vehicle for three stars in the popular backstage melodrama."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":42,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2008/04/28/theater/reviews/28coun.html","d":"2008-04-28","q":"And for whatever reason, everyone in “The Country Girl” seems to be operating on his or her own isolating frequency."},{"cn":"Eric March","o":"Theater Life","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":3,"u":"https://theaterlife.com/the-country-girl/","d":"2008-05-29","q":"The credible production lacks the histrionics necessary to fire the melodrama."}],"au":{"score":58,"designation":"Disliking","sources":{"mz":{"s":58,"c":5,"sr":2.9}}},"ta":"242 W 45th St, New York, NY 10036","pd":"2008-04-03","ca":[{"n":"Morgan Freeman","r":"Frank Elgin"},{"n":"Peter Gallagher","r":"Bernie Dodd"},{"n":"Frances McDormand","r":"Georgie Elgin"},{"n":"Remy Auberjonois","r":"Paul Unger"},{"n":"Anna Camp","r":"Nancy Stoddard"},{"n":"Joe Roland","r":"Ralph"},{"n":"Lucas Caleb Rooney","r":"Larry"},{"n":"Chip Zien","r":"Phil Cook"}]}